CORE
main.cpp
--cpp17
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ unqualified member find resolves to C::find, not arg-class member: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG must FAIL: FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
^.*does not uniquely resolve.*$
--
N5008 [basic.lookup.argdep]/3.1: when ordinary unqualified lookup of a name
finds the declaration of a class member, the associated namespaces/classes are
not considered (ADL is suppressed); ADL ([basic.lookup.argdep]/4) never
considers an associated class's member functions.  Fixed in
cpp_typecheck_resolvet::resolve: suppress the resolve_with_arguments ADL pass
when ordinary lookup already found a class member (except for operator names,
which use [over.match.oper]'s separate candidate-gathering).  This unblocks the
src/util/xml.h `xmlt::get_element` -> `find(element)` vs `std::basic_string::find`
ambiguity.  Non-vacuous (assertion 2 must FAIL).
